# Main-menu local mail notices: software evidence

Issue [#239](https://github.com/gonz0w/faction-bbs/issues/239) covers the
visit-local notice choice described in the [member guide](../../../docs/main-menu-mail.md)
and [technical handoff](../../main-menu-mail.md). This record concerns manual,
locked or stale local snapshots; it does not establish that a home is current.

## Observations

Source-bound host and NetBSD classic and Unicode main-menu routes exercised the
choice with Files disabled. They observed a real TCP refusal at the home, unknown
status after wrong or cancelled unlock, a stale snapshot after successful graceful
lock, consent clearing and re-enabling as unknown, and notices off on a new visit.
The routes returned to the same SSH session. Saved logical mail state before and
after was equal; ciphertext equality was checked in memory by the executed source.
The source-bound board I/O and database, store and log scans found no selected
private markers. These scans are not an independent historical rescan of board
files.

Separate host and NetBSD shared Files routes observed the same visit-local consent
and snapshot across both entry points. Existing inbox, correspondents, reply and
main-menu compatibility controls returned successfully on both systems. The
[result record](results.json) identifies the selected sources, routes and other
observations. The offline [evidence guard](../../../tools/check_menu_mail_notices_evidence.py)
validates saved route, build, source and cleanup records; it does not rerun the
original sessions. The guarded [finalizer](integration/finalize.py) requires
private original-capture review and a scan of the same publication selection.
Acceptance of the final record also requires actual stop and removal of owned
fixtures and proof that the saved playground remains intact.

## Preserved failures and limits

The first native raw-PTY tests reached their visible steps but timed out during
test-worker teardown. The corrected test harness drains shutdown output while
waiting; it retains the original assertions and deadline. The original failure and
both source variants are preserved. An initial route probe also failed because its
protocol counter expected LF while the real PTY sent CR. Its failure and the
substantive correction are separate from product behavior RED.

The original five-test probe's source was recovered from independently checked
contemporaneous literal session inputs. Its missing-module RED was one failed
loader test, not five executed assertion bodies. A later O/E edit is not a
retroactive RED. Preservation gaps and rejected setups do not establish a
behavioral failure.

Original traces and generated private material require private review; raw
captures, credentials, keys and mail stores are not publication material. The
final record must report the actual scan and cleanup receipts before claiming
publication or teardown. The saved owner playground remains stopped and intact.
These are bounded software-fixture observations, not physical hardware,
capacity, security certification, graphical, production or routing-quality claims.
